<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Live Equivocation ~ the one attack detection cannot fix, built last

The federated-mesh collision (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/field-collision">> #the-mesh-field) named the roadmap's biggest exposure. This meme holds it OPEN for later work — the outside negentropy to gather, the fiction stories to run, and the ruling the operator leans toward (pull recovery-quorum FORWARD beside the sensorium).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-two-thieves>>

!! Two thieves, and they are not the same

* ''The DEAD-key thief'' breaks a drawer and finds a key you STOPPED using. ''KERI pre-rotation already defeats them'' — the key they hold cannot authorize its own succession; you rotated past it. The FACE rung handles this.
* ''The LIVING-key thief'' captures your key WHILE YOU ARE STILL SIGNING WITH IT — a compromised phone, a coerced signature, a shared cabal-name one member turns. Now there are ''two of you presenting one name in real time,'' and both hold a valid key. KERI states plainly: a live current+next capture has ''NO administrative recovery from keys alone.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-blind-spot>>

!! Detection and recovery are each other's blind spot

The sensorium ''DETECTS'' the equivocation — it sees two of you. But ''seeing it does not RESTORE you'': you are now a name with two valid claimants and no key-only way to prove which is true. Only ''recovery'' — a trusted quorum re-keying you under a fresh root — puts you back. And worse: a living thief who ALSO controls enough carriage can make the ambient itself lie (the diffusion-sensing fool — a well-connected corner reads as "the whole mesh moved"), so ''abstain fires and detection goes blind EXACTLY when the attack is live.'' Detection cannot fix what it sees; recovery cannot act on what it cannot see. ''Built apart, the living hijack has neither in time.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-human-stakes>>

!! Who this is for (the irl tension)

The journalist whose source-protecting identity is seized under duress. The activist whose shared movement-name a defector turns. The family cabal one compromised device betrays. For all of them, ''detection that only says "there are two of you" is a diagnosis with no cure.'' Recovery beside detection — a quorum that re-keys the moment the equivocation is seen — is the cure, and it must be ''already standing when the attack lands,'' not built two milestones later.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/elyncia-as-qa>>

!! Elyncia is the first QA world (fiction as the harness)

Real cabals with real stakes do not exist yet, so abstract unit tests cannot feel the tension the mechanics must survive. ''The fiction is the first QA environment.'' Telarus the wild-mage lit Elyncia's DreamNet ~500 years before modern day (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/characters/primary-characters/telarus">>), and 500 years of rise · dormancy · revival · betrayal · inheritance are a scenario library the mechanics can be RUN against. A cabal name grafted across generations; a wild-mage's DreamNet identity live-hijacked mid-working; a shrine-realm slept a century then woken for a rite; a Dread-Pirate-Roberts-style name presented by a rotating crew — each is a load-bearing user story for the ahi-kā reading, the handle-KEL, the recovery-quorum, and this exposure. The `AHI_KA_500YR` defaults (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ahi-ka">>) are calibrated to this world; tune them by running its events. ''irl tension + fiction series = the QA env.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/owed>>

!! Owed to later spirits (the research queue)

# ''Outside negentropy'' — collide the live-equivocation case against the field: KERI/vLEI live-key recovery ceremonies, threshold re-keying (FROST resharing), social-recovery wallets (Argent, safe-guardians), duress/coercion-resistant schemes (deniable keys, canaries), MPC custody rotation. What does anyone deployed do when a key is stolen WHILE ALIVE?
# ''Fiction user stories'' — mine the Elyncia canon for concrete hijack/inheritance/dormancy scenarios and render each as a QA vector against the mechanics.
# ''The ruling'' — the operator leans PULL RECOVERY-QUORUM FORWARD beside the sensorium (co-design detection + recovery). A later pass confirms the sequence and the recovery-rotation ⊥ equivocation-fork distinction a watcher must draw. See <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/recovery-registration">> and <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/handoff">>.
# ''ANSWERED at primary source — the recovery-field survey.'' No deployed or researched system recovers from a fully live key capture using key material alone; the residual (an attacker holding current+next, or a full threshold within one epoch, ''acting inside the window'') is universal. KERI states it: "there is no recovery mechanism once the keys for the root control authority have been fully captured," and its superseding-rule A1 (a non-delegated rotation cannot supersede another rotation) makes a root-level live capture terminal. The ONLY lever that touches a genuinely live key is a ''time-lock + veto window'', deployed everywhere: did:plc's priority-ordered rotation keys + a ''72-hour window'' in which a colder higher-authority key rewrites history, clobbering the lower-authority key; Nostr NIP-41's pre-committed successor + OpenTimestamps anchor + a ''30-day public contest window''; social-recovery wallets' guardian time-lock+veto (Argent 36h, Safe 28d) — which confirm the civic keel (''recovery quorum IS the impersonation quorum''). Duress schemes (GrapheneOS wipe, LUKS-nuke, hidden volumes) only ''destroy or signal, never rotate an already-copied key'', and all fall to observe-first suppression — a duress key denies future access or raises an alarm; it does not recover you. The residual is inherent, not a shortfall to engineer away.
# ''CONSTRUCTIVE — CHURP makes the GRAFT a share-refresh, bounding the living-thief window on the FROST tier.'' CHURP (Maram et al., eprint 2019/017) is dynamic-committee proactive secret sharing: at each handoff the committee re-shares so ''shares from epoch //e// become useless in epoch //e+1//, while the secret and its public key are unchanged'', with members joining/leaving and threshold //t// changing at the handoff — mechanism-for-mechanism the GRAFT (`mintHandleGraft` rolls the owner-set + threshold, `prefix`/`handleKeyDid` fixed). Today the k-of-n is a MULTISIG (`graftSigs` gathers //t// distinct Ed25519 signatures), with no shared secret to refresh; CHURP earns its keep only on the ''FROST/veiled-Circle branch'' (the-veil-ladder), where a private Circle signs as ONE invisible key — there a captured share ''dies at the next graft, public handle key unchanged, no rotation visible on the wire.'' A scheduled graft cadence, paced by FfzClock to the adversary's measured creep, is then a proactive-refresh interval. Take the ''OFF-CHAIN construction only'' — CHURP's dispute path resolves on-chain; route accusation to the duplicity-proof + veto (`detectDuplicity`, `foldPersonaContests`), never a chain. The residual stays inherent: PSS refreshes a STANDING secret and does nothing once an adversary holds ≥//t// shares WITHIN one epoch (they reconstruct) — it shrinks the window, it does not close the simultaneous-quorum seizure the two-thieves already name.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/what-decides-it>>

!! What this path needs before anyone can rule it (operator, 2026-09-13)

''The PULL-FORWARD lean stands SET ASIDE — not the plan.'' Sequencing recovery-quorum construction beside
the sensorium reads reasonable and rests on nothing measured. The path DEFERS until the infrastructure
stands to test it, and defers cleanly: nothing downstream waits on it, and the residual it addresses
(§#/owed) reads as ''inherent'' rather than as a shortfall anyone is failing to engineer away.

!!! The one number that decides the shape

''A time-lock + veto window is the only lever that touches a genuinely live key'' (§#/owed, answered at
primary source). Every deployed system picks a duration — did:plc 72 hours, Nostr NIP-41 30 days, Argent
36 hours, Safe 28 days — and ''a window shorter than the time a watcher takes to NOTICE is theatre'': the
thief acts, nobody contests in time, and the ceremony ratifies the capture while looking rigorous.

So the ruling waits on ''measured detection latency'': how long, in practice, between a duplicity landing
on a board and a watcher folding it into a contest. Nobody has measured it, because the organ that would
measure it does not stand.

!!! What must stand first, and what each one buys

# ''A fully running sensorium stack.'' The detection half. `detectDuplicity` folds a proof today, but no
live plane WATCHES for one across real traffic — detection latency has no observer, so its distribution
has never been sampled. With the stack up, the number becomes an experiment rather than an estimate.
# ''A fully set-up meshpalace.'' The memory half. A latency distribution wants HISTORY, not one reading:
the window must clear the tail, never the median, and only a durable telemetry plane holds enough
observations to see a tail at all.

''Both, together, answer one question'': what window clears the observed detection tail with margin? That
number picks the mechanism — a short window suits an automatic priority-key clobber (did:plc's shape), a
long one suits a public contest (NIP-41's shape), and the two want different code.

!!! What a later pass should NOT re-derive

''The residual stays inherent.'' An adversary holding current+next, or a full threshold inside one epoch,
acting within the window, defeats every deployed scheme — KERI states it outright. A pass that arrives
hoping to close that hole will spend itself; the work is BOUNDING the window, never closing it.

''CHURP bounds the FROST branch and only that branch'' (§#/owed): it earns its keep where a private Circle
signs as one invisible key, and buys nothing against today's multisig graft, which holds no shared secret
to refresh.

<<~/ahu>>

